# Mount Baratok: the cairn on the summit (prop) and the lightning ridge (random event, data/random_encounters/baratok_slopes.json).

~ cairn
Narrator: A cairn of flat grey stones, waist-high, stacked with a care nobody spends on a trail marker. The stones are warm. Snow melts on them as it lands.
if flag.mordenkainen_eyes_read
Narrator: This is what the old man's eyes kept going to, every time a word got away from him.
endif
if flag.baratok_ward_found
Narrator: The ward is still there, coiled in its ring of frost, but now you know where its edges are, and so does it.
else
interject class:wizard: Somebody warded this, and not for show. Look at the frost around it. It's in a perfect ring.
endif
* Unstack the stones. -> cairn_open
* Leave it standing. -> END

~ cairn_open
set mordenkainen_spellbook_found
if not quest.the_mad_mage >= book_found
quest the_mad_mage book_found
endif
Narrator: Under the last stone, wrapped in oilcloth gone stiff with cold, lies a fat spellbook bound in grey leather, and tucked inside its cover two loose scrolls, written fast. The hand is strong and impatient. The capital letters all have a little hook.
give spell_scroll_level_1 2
interject name:ratatoille: That is a master's book. Not a clever student's. A master's. Somebody else hold it, my hands are shaking.
-> END

~ lightning_ridge
cutscene lightning_ridge
set baratok_storm_seen
Narrator: The trail crosses a bare ridge as the light goes, and a single cloud, no bigger than a barn, slides up over Mount Baratok on its own and stops overhead.
Narrator: Lightning comes down, once, into a ring of black glass on the ridge where it has plainly come down every evening for years. The thunder rolls off down the valley and doesn't come back.
* [Arcana DC 14] What made that cloud? -> ridge_arcana | ridge_arcana_fail
* Keep walking, quickly. -> END

~ ridge_arcana
Narrator: It's a spell, not weather: a great one, cast once and left running, like a clock somebody wound and forgot. Whoever told the sky to strike here every evening never told it to stop, and the work is so good it hasn't faltered once.
interject class:wizard: That's not a storm. That's a reminder. Somebody set it to go off every night, like a bell.
-> END

~ ridge_arcana_fail
Narrator: It looks like weather. It smells like weather. It is far too punctual to be weather.
-> END
